message: 'If you use Unlock the Lab or its materials, please cite it as below.'
title: 'Unlock the Lab: Your guide to reading science like a scientist'
type: software
authors:
    - family-names: Bernabeu
      given-names: Pablo
      orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1083-2460'
version: 2.1.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19153148
url: 'https://unlock-the-lab.web.app'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/pablobernabeu/Unlock_the_Lab'
license:
    - MIT
    - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
    A web application for science-literacy workshops. Participants read
    fictional but realistic study summaries, rate their quality on a 1-7 scale
    against a six-criterion rubric, predict the ratings of other participants and
    receive expert feedback. A public dashboard shows aggregate results, and the
    pseudonymous data support research on how people evaluate scientific evidence.
keywords:
    - science literacy
    - research quality
    - critical thinking
    - peer assessment
    - education
